HST-Aligned MW–M31 Merger Simulation
Class & Dataclass Documentation Sheet

Dataclasses
1. SimulationConfig

Fields only (no methods):

softening_length

timestep

n_steps

phasespace_bins

snapshot_stride

enable_energy_tracking

enable_angular_momentum_tracking

save_snapshots

Description:
Container for all numerical and diagnostic configuration parameters controlling the simulation, integration cadence, and post-processing behavior.

Operations performed:

Supplies global numerical parameters to:

Gravity solver

Integrator

Diagnostics pipeline

Controls snapshot cadence and optional disk output

Acts as a single source of truth for reproducibility

2. GalaxyComponent

Fields only (no methods):

name

component_id

total_mass

particle_count

scale_length

scale_height

component_type

Description:
Abstract representation of a galactic structural component (disk or halo), used to parameterize initial condition generation.

Operations performed:

Defines mass, size, and resolution for particle sampling

Supplies metadata to the initial condition factory

Encodes component identity via component_id

3. Snapshot

Fields only (no methods):

state

time

step

Description:
Immutable record of the full N-body system state at a specific simulation time.

Operations performed:

Stores particle phase-space data

Enables time-ordered diagnostics

Acts as atomic unit for trajectory analysis

Core Simulation Classes
4. InitialConditionFactory

Static methods:

hernquist_halo(component)

exponential_disk(component)

Description:
Factory class responsible for sampling initial particle distributions for galactic components.

Operations performed:

Samples spatial distributions for disks and halos

Assigns masses and component IDs

Produces standardized (N, 8) state arrays

Initializes approximate kinematics (disk rotation, halo placeholders)

5. GravitySolver

Methods:

__init__(softening)

accelerations(pos, m)

Description:
Direct-summation Newtonian gravity solver with Plummer softening.

Operations performed:

Computes pairwise gravitational accelerations

Applies softening to suppress numerical divergences

Serves as the force backend for the integrator

6. LeapfrogIntegrator

Methods:

__init__(solver)

step(state, dt)

Description:
Second-order symplectic leapfrog integrator for collisionless N-body dynamics.

Operations performed:

Advances particle positions and velocities in time

Preserves phase-space structure to leading order

Minimizes secular energy drift

7. Trajectory

Methods:

__init__()

add(state, time, step)

times()

Description:
Container for the time-ordered evolution of the simulation.

Operations performed:

Stores snapshots at configurable cadence

Provides access to simulation timeline

Acts as the backbone for all diagnostics

Phase-Space & Diagnostics
8. PhaseSpaceMetrics

Methods:

__init__(bins)

density(state)

Description:
Computes coarse-grained phase-space density via multidimensional binning.

Operations performed:

Constructs 6D phase-space histograms

Normalizes densities for entropy calculation

Implements observationally motivated coarse-graining

9. EntropyEvolution

Methods:

__init__(bins)

entropy(state)

series(traj)

Description:
Tracks coarse-grained phase-space entropy as a function of time.

Operations performed:

Computes Shannon entropy from binned phase space

Generates entropy time series

Quantifies phase-space irreversibility

